#
# Tell the driver what the modules in the cages are as soon as the system is up, so that a cage's
# port reports its module's medium and not "unknown" (#533): at once from what was read before
# this boot, then from the modules themselves (scripts/xgs/transceivers.py). The second is
# detached, so the boot never waits for it. On the XGS 3300 it is the coprocessor's console, which
# takes its time and is busy at boot with the other plugins' first reads, so it is asked again
# every 20 s for up to three minutes; the plugin's five-minute cron entry reads them after that.

T=/usr/local/opnsense/scripts/xgs/transceivers.py
[ -x "${T}" ] || exit 0
"${T}" apply > /dev/null 2>&1
/usr/sbin/daemon -f "${T}" collect --tries 9
exit 0
